sequenceDiagram
    participant D as Point-in-time data
    participant E as Specialists
    participant C as Controller
    participant X as Paper execution
    participant O as Delayed outcome
    participant M as Reliability memory

    D->>E: Features available by close t
    E->>C: Forecasts and calibrated uncertainty
    C->>C: Select, combine, request, fallback, or abstain
    C->>X: Eligible action no earlier than t+1
    Note over C,M: No future target can enter memory
    O-->>M: Outcome arrives after forecast horizon
    M-->>C: Update only under predeclared protocol

